  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The strongest completed result is config_019, a multimodal multiprofile model with PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion, reaching 0.639 accuracy and 0.620 F1, above the best RNA-only avgpool model and the concat-fusion multimodal model. RNA-only evidence also suggests avgpool is preferable to transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion appears slightly better than concat, so those settings should be kept. The main remaining uncertainty in this promising direction is the image encoder: ResNet50 was weak as an image-only model, yet it still helped in multimodal fusion. Testing config_025 changes only the image encoder to ViT-L while preserving the best-known RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion. This isolates the effect of image representation, exploits the current best configuration, and has high potential immediate value by clarifying whether a stronger image encoder can improve the leading multimodal setup."
}

